/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  surfacetension01 -- THE MEASURED CURVE BESIDE THE ESTIMATE (DEV.md 4c C328).

  For each of five liquids (methanol, ethanol, 1-propanol, triethanolamine,
  n-hexane) the sigma(T) of two models is evaluated at three temperatures
  inside the window the record declares:

    StoredCorrelation   sigma = A (1 - T/Tc)^n + B (1 - T/Tc)^(n+1), read from
                        the component's own `surfaceTension {}` block.  The
                        numbers are a regression Choupo made on every
                        laboratory the ThermoML archive holds for the pure
                        liquid (A, n fitted; B = 0; the largest relative error
                        over the data is the record's own fitGradeMaxRelative
                        Error_pct: 4.3 % methanol, 4.0 % ethanol, 3.9 %
                        1-propanol, 3.6 % triethanolamine, 2.8 % n-hexane).
                        It is graded inSample and reviewed by nobody; the
                        measured points are not stored in this tree.
    BrockBird           the corresponding-states estimate from Tc, Pc and Tb
                        (Reid-Prausnitz-Poling eq. 12-3.5), no sigma datum.

  Read the pairs: n-hexane, a hydrocarbon, is where Brock-Bird works (its
  largest deviation from the fitted curve over the data is 3.8 %); methanol
  (108 %), ethanol (88 %), 1-propanol (72 %) and triethanolamine (76 %) are
  where it does not.  A property op prints sigma [N/m]; the deviation of the
  estimate from the stored curve is brockBird / stored - 1, read off the two
  columns of each pair.  The golden master locks every sigma at reltol 1e-5.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name        sigma_methanol_280K_stored;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 280 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { methanol 1.0; } }
        thermo      { transport { interface { surfaceTension { model StoredCorrelation; } } } }
        properties  ( surface_tension );
    }
    {
        name        sigma_methanol_280K_brockBird;
        type        propertyPoint;
        state       { T 280 K;  P 1 bar;  composition { methanol 1.0; } }
        thermo      { transport { interface { surfaceTension { model BrockBird; } } } }
